didn't have to do anything.

01:15:24.240 --> 01:15:25.810
Yeah, I mean, you had
to keep strumming along

01:15:25.810 --> 01:15:27.613
but like, he was, that was a,

01:15:27.613 --> 01:15:30.177
that was a very easy moment to like,

01:15:30.177 --> 01:15:32.920
"Okay, there's no pressure
of performance for me."

01:15:32.920 --> 01:15:35.200
I'm like, "I can," I was looking.

01:15:35.200 --> 01:15:37.120
I was looking at how
much fun you were having.

01:15:37.120 --> 01:15:40.070
He was into it, it's
like that's the moment

01:15:40.070 --> 01:15:43.760
where I was really
savoring and taking it in.

01:15:43.760 --> 01:15:48.560
And we talked about it on stage and like,

01:15:48.560 --> 01:15:51.460
that, it became the, us experiencing it

01:15:51.460 --> 01:15:53.490
became the experience for the audience.

01:15:53.490 --> 01:15:54.810
So like they became a part of it

01:15:54.810 --> 01:15:57.590
and it was just a cycle of energy.

01:15:57.590 --> 01:15:59.880
Yeah, it's it's weird because it's like,

01:15:59.880 --> 01:16:02.610
it's the one moment I
can point to on here,

01:16:02.610 --> 01:16:06.520
where I can actually
remember what it felt like,

01:16:06.520 --> 01:16:07.353
Yeah.

01:16:07.353 --> 01:16:08.186
Whereas everything else,

01:16:08.186 --> 01:16:09.860
I can kind of remember what happened

01:16:09.860 --> 01:16:11.723
and how it makes me feel now.

01:16:12.610 --> 01:16:15.080
But I can almost like transport
myself back to that moment,

01:16:15.080 --> 01:16:18.120
I was like, it registered.

01:16:18.120 --> 01:16:20.387
I was like, "Oh, this is,

01:16:20.387 --> 01:16:23.570
"this moment is hitting me right now."

01:16:23.570 --> 01:16:25.890
Whereas typically, you're
doing something like camping

01:16:25.890 --> 01:16:27.090
with your kid or whatever.

01:16:27.090 --> 01:16:28.590
And you're like, this
whole thing is awesome.

01:16:28.590 --> 01:16:29.877
And I'm having a great time.
Yeah

01:16:29.877 --> 01:16:31.720
And this a moment where we're
listening to this podcast,

01:16:31.720 --> 01:16:33.930
and I'm realizing that
this is a good thing,

01:16:33.930 --> 01:16:35.660
we're bonding, et cetera.

01:16:35.660 --> 01:16:38.400
But it really is the sort of
taking it and distilling it

01:16:38.400 --> 01:16:40.030
later as a memory and that,

01:16:40.030 --> 01:16:42.370
but it was like, no, it was in the moment.

01:16:42.370 --> 01:16:43.570
Yeah.
And it really only happened,

01:16:43.570 --> 01:16:45.243
the is the one I can point to.

01:16:45.243 --> 01:16:49.060
It's the one time I can I can
point to that being the case.

01:16:49.060 --> 01:16:52.143
Well, and I mean, when
you talk about the ther,

01:16:52.143 --> 01:16:54.220
you know, when you talk
about therapy and like,

01:16:54.220 --> 01:16:56.010
being able to get more in
touch with your feelings,

01:16:56.010 --> 01:16:57.730
I do think that's an aspect of it.

01:16:57.730 --> 01:16:59.830
You know, I feel like they were--

01:16:59.830 --> 01:17:01.340
I think so.
I feel like

01:17:01.340 --> 01:17:04.130
there are moments throughout
the list when I can,

01:17:04.130 --> 01:17:08.070
I can re-access the feelings I had

01:17:08.070 --> 01:17:10.540
and feel a bit emotional about a number

01:17:10.540 --> 01:17:12.140
of these things on the list but,

01:17:13.100 --> 01:17:14.507
yeah, that I mean that was a special one,

01:17:14.507 --> 01:17:18.040
and it's cool because it you know,

01:17:18.040 --> 01:17:20.650
people talk, when you
talk about country music,

01:17:20.650 --> 01:17:24.900
or like, performance venues,
it's like it pops up, you know,

01:17:24.900 --> 01:17:26.797
watch the Ken Burns
documentary on country music

01:17:26.797 --> 01:17:29.310
and it's, it's so much
of it is about the Ryman,

01:17:29.310 --> 01:17:31.570
it's like, "Wow, I've
performed on that stage."

01:17:31.570 --> 01:17:32.930
You know, it's like,
Yeah.

01:17:32.930 --> 01:17:34.710
It comes out of the woodwork a lot.

01:17:34.710 --> 01:17:38.600
So it's, there's always an occasion to

01:17:38.600 --> 01:17:40.640
be grateful that we were
on that stage again,

01:17:40.640 --> 01:17:41.720
which is really cool.

01:17:41.720 --> 01:17:42.553
Yeah.

01:17:43.620 --> 01:17:47.840
Yeah, so that's, that I mean,

01:17:47.840 --> 01:17:52.840
that was, that was a number
one worthy experience for me.

01:17:52.930 --> 01:17:55.150
But if I'm going to get to my number one,

01:17:55.150 --> 01:17:58.960
this one's, this one's related to Christy.

01:17:58.960 --> 01:18:03.360
This is a milestone that she experienced

01:18:03.360 --> 01:18:07.593
that for me was just
vicariously through her.

01:18:08.675 --> 01:18:10.920
Excuse me.

01:18:10.920 --> 01:18:13.140
So, a little backstory,
I'm trying to remember

01:18:13.140 --> 01:18:15.120
how much of this I've
shared on the podcast?

01:18:15.120 --> 01:18:17.230
I think I've only shared.

01:18:17.230 --> 01:18:20.110
I've shared the fact
that like, Christy has,

01:18:20.110 --> 01:18:23.193
she suffers from post-concussion syndrome.

01:18:24.527 --> 01:18:28.490
So it's basically she has daily symptoms,

01:18:28.490 --> 01:18:33.490
invisible symptoms that
originated over three years ago

01:18:34.420 --> 01:18:38.290
when she was walking
into the grocery store

01:18:38.290 --> 01:18:40.300
and she stepped up on a curb.

01:18:40.300 --> 01:18:43.233
And just that simple step up.

01:18:44.980 --> 01:18:46.270
She hit her head,

01:18:46.270 --> 01:18:49.183
the very top of her head
on a tree limb that,

01:18:50.200 --> 01:18:51.830
then she sustained a concussion.

01:18:51.830 --> 01:18:52.880
She was never knocked out.

01:18:52.880 --> 01:18:54.150
She never lost consciousness,

01:18:54.150 --> 01:18:57.203
but she sat back down in the
car and gathered herself.

01:18:58.250 --> 01:19:00.870
Ultimately went to the Emergency Room

01:19:00.870 --> 01:19:05.270
and got got checked out
and certified as okay,

01:19:05.270 --> 01:19:07.180
but that she did sustain a concussion

01:19:07.180 --> 01:19:08.600
and it needed to watch it.

01:19:08.600 --> 01:19:10.990
A couple of weeks later,

01:19:10.990 --> 01:19:14.230
which turns out is common with concussions

01:19:14.230 --> 01:19:18.240
that there was like,
and she took a nosedive.

01:19:18.240 --> 01:19:20.660
Metaphorically, I mean,
in terms of her symptoms

01:19:20.660 --> 01:19:23.780
got a whole lot worse after two weeks.

01:19:23.780 --> 01:19:28.049
And then, lo and behold, fast forward,

01:19:28.049 --> 01:19:30.700
three years later, she still has,

01:19:30.700 --> 01:19:32.800
like I said, symptoms every single day

01:19:32.800 --> 01:19:35.423
of what she calls brain
fog, where it's like,

01:19:36.307 --> 01:19:39.880
like your head is floating,
you have trouble concentrating.

01:19:39.880 --> 01:19:43.720
She's had a lot of issues with balance,

01:19:43.720 --> 01:19:48.570
and it's just dramatically
impacted her moment by moment,

01:19:48.570 --> 01:19:50.693
quality of life.

01:19:52.310 --> 01:19:54.943
And it's one of those things
that it probably took,

01:19:56.140 --> 01:19:58.530
it took over a year to come to grips with

01:19:58.530 --> 01:20:03.530
the fact that she has this
condition, this catch all label,

01:20:03.570 --> 01:20:05.470
where you really don't
know what's going on

01:20:05.470 --> 01:20:08.040
within the mystery of the brain.

01:20:08.040 --> 01:20:11.950
And there's nothing you
can do to just fix it.

01:20:11.950 --> 01:20:14.100
You know, there's lots
of things you can try.

01:20:14.100 --> 01:20:16.873
And she was trying all types of things.

01:20:18.910 --> 01:20:23.910
But she, she went on a
friend of ours podcast,

01:20:24.150 --> 01:20:26.250
and I think that's, that
may have been the first time

01:20:26.250 --> 01:20:28.390
that I mentioned any of this was when,

01:20:28.390 --> 01:20:30.567
as a recommendation, I said,

01:20:30.567 --> 01:20:34.207
"You should listen to the
'Ask Science Mike' podcast,

01:20:34.207 --> 01:20:36.437
"Episode 180, called

01:20:36.437 --> 01:20:39.190
"'Living with brain injury
with Christy Neal.'"

01:20:39.190 --> 01:20:43.053
So if you wanna look that
up, she in her own words,

01:20:44.070 --> 01:20:46.290
shares her entire story.

01:20:46.290 --> 01:20:50.801
I think that was in, that was
the middle of the year that,

01:20:50.801 --> 01:20:54.053
so up into that point, you get her story.

01:20:55.430 --> 01:20:57.598
So again, I recommend
that you listen to that.

01:20:57.598 --> 01:21:00.687
If you know someone who's
sustained a brain injury

01:21:00.687 --> 01:21:04.120
or you are suffering from one listen to

01:21:04.120 --> 01:21:06.133
Ask Science Mike, Episode 180.

01:21:07.720 --> 01:21:12.050
So she, you know, I was so
proud of her in that moment

01:21:12.050 --> 01:21:14.980
where she was able to share her story

01:21:14.980 --> 01:21:19.540
and redeem a lot of the
pain that she's experienced

01:21:19.540 --> 01:21:21.970
over the years and
hardship she's been through

01:21:21.970 --> 01:21:26.030
in being able to share the
strength that she's found

01:21:26.030 --> 01:21:30.763
in that, in the midst of
such a difficult condition.

01:21:32.760 --> 01:21:37.220
And the response has been
overwhelmingly positive.

01:21:37.220 --> 01:21:39.470
And she, it was so, she was so encouraged.

01:21:39.470 --> 01:21:41.120
We're all very encouraged to hear

01:21:41.960 --> 01:21:43.333
everyone's response to it.

01:21:45.570 --> 01:21:48.990
And then, she was doing lots of things

01:21:48.990 --> 01:21:51.120
and going to see all types of doctors

01:21:51.120 --> 01:21:55.000
to try to continue to
get better and slowly,

01:21:55.000 --> 01:22:00.000
very slowly over time she,
she's seen gradual improvement.

01:22:00.070 --> 01:22:05.070
But, I have, I still have an innate sense

01:22:05.170 --> 01:22:08.580
if I go into a space, that's really loud,

01:22:08.580 --> 01:22:12.100
I kind of know the
decibel level with which

01:22:12.100 --> 01:22:13.900
Christy can't be there.

01:22:13.900 --> 01:22:18.000
You know, that like she,
there's too much sensory input.

01:22:18.000 --> 01:22:22.930
Or I can look at her face and tell when it

01:22:22.930 --> 01:22:24.390
there's too much going on.

01:22:24.390 --> 01:22:26.560
She's having a brain overload,
that she needs a break,

01:22:26.560 --> 01:22:27.700
or that she needs to step away

01:22:27.700 --> 01:22:29.630
from the group that we're with.

01:22:29.630 --> 01:22:32.170
I'm sure you, you know,
you and Jessie also

01:22:32.170 --> 01:22:34.500
have picked up on a lot of this like,

01:22:34.500 --> 01:22:36.660
but at a certain point,

01:22:36.660 --> 01:22:38.010
it's the type of thing that

01:22:39.300 --> 01:22:41.170
you don't wanna keep asking every day,

01:22:41.170 --> 01:22:42.110
how are you feeling?

01:22:42.110 --> 01:22:45.249
Because every day it's, I feel,

01:22:45.249 --> 01:22:49.050
I feel like I feel the
same, or I feel horrible.

01:22:49.050 --> 01:22:50.510
I feel worse.

01:22:50.510 --> 01:22:52.930
There's never, it doesn't seem like

01:22:52.930 --> 01:22:54.300
there's ever many days where it's like

01:22:54.300 --> 01:22:57.430
I feel better, a little bit better.

01:22:57.430 --> 01:23:01.820
It's this trajectory that if
you map it over three years,

01:23:01.820 --> 01:23:03.920
you realize I can do things that I

01:23:03.920 --> 01:23:05.870
that I used to couldn't do.

01:23:05.870 --> 01:23:08.160
But there's never one day
that you ask and decide,

01:23:08.160 --> 01:23:10.763
well, that's amazing,
I actually feel fine.

01:23:11.660 --> 01:23:12.720
It's just didn't happen.

01:23:12.720 --> 01:23:14.320
It never happens.

01:23:14.320 --> 01:23:17.100
So at a certain point,
you start, you know,

01:23:17.100 --> 01:23:21.400
you stop asking because
you don't, you know,

01:23:21.400 --> 01:23:25.090
it almost it feels like it
makes it worse to ask when,

01:23:25.090 --> 01:23:29.870
after years of the answer
being something negative,

01:23:29.870 --> 01:23:31.180
that you're gonna get that again.

01:23:31.180 --> 01:23:34.890
So, it's kinda sparing
her having articulate

01:23:34.890 --> 01:23:36.750
by asking and she doesn't wanna share,

01:23:36.750 --> 01:23:40.640
and she puts on she, she
puts on the positive face

01:23:40.640 --> 01:23:44.383
and she she goes on with her life because,

01:23:46.420 --> 01:23:49.180
because she's got the strength to do it.

01:23:49.180 --> 01:23:53.720
But then there's this there's a silent,

01:23:53.720 --> 01:23:55.170
you know, there's a silent condition,

01:23:55.170 --> 01:23:57.700
that's with her every second
and it's not the type of,

01:23:57.700 --> 01:24:01.070
so, I mean, that's, and then we went

01:24:01.070 --> 01:24:02.140
when we went to Thailand,

01:24:02.140 --> 01:24:05.140
and honestly, I think
one of the reasons why

01:24:07.280 --> 01:24:11.877
the Thailand trip in retrospect
is like lower on my list,

01:24:11.877 --> 01:24:13.080
to kind of make a little sense of that,

01:24:13.080 --> 01:24:18.080
is the fact that it was difficult for her,

01:24:18.140 --> 01:24:20.770
when her symptoms kind of flared up,

01:24:20.770 --> 01:24:23.090
especially when we got back.

01:24:23.090 --> 01:24:25.050
So from when we got back from Thailand,

01:24:25.050 --> 01:24:26.750
for weeks, it was like,

01:24:26.750 --> 01:24:30.680
it felt like she had
taken a lot of steps back,

01:24:30.680 --> 01:24:34.653
like she was feeling
horrible every single day.

01:24:35.870 --> 01:24:38.130
Again, there's no, you can't
point to any one thing,

01:24:38.130 --> 01:24:41.110
but it's like there's,
maybe it's the time change.

01:24:41.110 --> 01:24:43.380
Maybe it's all the heat
that we endured there.

01:24:43.380 --> 01:24:45.680
It's like you really don't know.

01:24:45.680 --> 01:24:47.863
But she was just doing worse,

01:24:49.998 --> 01:24:52.680
and it, but it kind of led her

01:24:54.020 --> 01:24:57.240
to redouble her efforts
to find other things

01:24:57.240 --> 01:25:00.600
that she could try in order to

01:25:00.600 --> 01:25:02.203
to experience some relief.

01:25:03.260 --> 01:25:05.550
It was very discouraging when after,

01:25:05.550 --> 01:25:07.730
after two and a half years or more

01:25:07.730 --> 01:25:11.363
things are getting worse you
feel like, instead of better.

01:25:12.740 --> 01:25:14.660
But it's, you know, it is
tremendous credit to her

01:25:14.660 --> 01:25:18.367
that she, that she started
going to new places and,

01:25:18.367 --> 01:25:21.370
and changing her regimen.

01:25:21.370 --> 01:25:25.890
One of the things that became
a part of her regimen was

01:25:25.890 --> 01:25:27.840
getting in a hyperbaric chamber,

01:25:27.840 --> 01:25:32.350
where you, they put you under 4 psi,

01:25:32.350 --> 01:25:34.240
and you stay in there for like an hour.

01:25:34.240 --> 01:25:36.080
They said do it like 40 hours

01:25:36.080 --> 01:25:36.950
and then we'll see how you're doing.

01:25:36.950 --> 01:25:40.550
You do 40 more hours in this tank.

01:25:40.550 --> 01:25:45.550
And the science says that when you're

01:25:45.730 --> 01:25:48.090
when you're put under
that amount of pressure

01:25:48.090 --> 01:25:53.090
it increases the the oxygen
concentration in your blood

01:25:55.170 --> 01:25:58.910
and basically enhances healing of whatever

01:25:58.910 --> 01:26:00.550
the case, of whatever needs healing.

01:26:00.550 --> 01:26:01.640
Right.

01:26:01.640 --> 01:26:03.100
Lot of athletes use it,

01:26:03.100 --> 01:26:04.730
a lot of people like burn injuries,

01:26:04.730 --> 01:26:05.873
all types of injuries.

01:26:08.301 --> 01:26:09.740
So that was a drastic thing.

01:26:09.740 --> 01:26:12.340
I mean I went on eBay and found a used one

01:26:12.340 --> 01:26:15.130
and bought it to put in our bedroom,

01:26:15.130 --> 01:26:16.380
so she could get into that thing,

01:26:16.380 --> 01:26:18.010
because with such a hectic lifestyle,

01:26:18.010 --> 01:26:19.660
like traveling halfway across LA

01:26:19.660 --> 01:26:22.770
to get in one and and pay
a fee to get in there,

01:26:22.770 --> 01:26:24.520
it just made more sense to get one.

01:26:25.360 --> 01:26:27.210
And I'm not going to say that is the thing

01:26:27.210 --> 01:26:30.730
that made her start to
feel better, solely,

01:26:30.730 --> 01:26:31.960
